  "title": "How Does the Internet Work?",
  "format": "main",
  "brief": {
    "audience": "curious kids and adults who use the internet daily but have never wondered what actually happens when they hit send",
    "learningGoal": "The viewer can explain that sending a video means splitting it into independently addressed packets forwarded one router-hop at a time with no reserved line and no master map, checked and reassembled by TCP, and carried mostly as light through glass fiber.",
    "hook": "Your video looks like it travels as one smooth beam straight to your friend's screen. It doesn't."
  },
